<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AllBlues-G-Theme" spTempo="108">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year: 	1959
Composer: 	Miles Davis
Lyricist: 	None — instrumental
Form: 	12-bar blues
Key: 	G minor

Recorded during the sessions for Miles Davis&apos;s
landmark album Kind of Blue, &quot;All Blues&quot; is a modal
blues that showcases the album&apos;s revolutionary
approach to improvisation based on scales rather
than chord changes. The piece features a distinctive
samba-influenced rhythm and the interplay between
Davis&apos;s trumpet and Cannonball Adderley&apos;s alto
saxophone, becoming one of the most recorded
and recognizable jazz compositions ever written.</spComments>
